//< An attribute whose name is mistyped (`#inlne`)
//<
//< The grammar takes any identifier as an attribute name, so an unknown one parses and would
//< silently do nothing (an unimplemented one such as `#no_mangle` too). It is matched against
//< `is_known_attribute` in `ksplc/sema/decl/attrs.kspls` and refused.
// EXPECT: unknown attribute '#inlne'

#inlne
fn f() {}

fn main(): I32
  f()
  return 0
